  "prefLabel": "Site 102.121 Blowdown event",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Site 102.121 “Blowdown event” means the automatic or manual venting of natural gas from a compressor or a section of pipeline taken off-line for maintenance or shutdown due to an emergency.\n\nSource. #11155, eff 8-16-16",
